## Definition

The terminal gts ARCHIVE writer \(the ONE canonical exit / narrow waist\): serialize the assembled carrier to generated/dist/gmeow\.gts\. GTS is exit\-only — produced here and nowhere else; every fold\-reading export leaf reads the carrier dataset off the gmeow:stage\-snapshot bundle, never these bytes\. The carrier is taken off the snapshot bundle \(no re\-assembly — the razor: transform transport→form at most once\), and the by\-reference blob archives are folded in alongside it: the fresh JSON\-Schema/OpenAPI \(gmeow:stage\-export\-json\-schema\), the compiled axiom surface \(gmeow:stage\-compile\-logic\), the native reasoning reports \(gmeow:stage\-reason\), the byte\-decorated RDF 1\.2 statement lanes \(gmeow:stage\-statements\), and the SHACL diagnostics SARIF/findings \(gmeow:stage\-validate\)\. The embedded executable\-docs 'try it' surface reasons over the object\-level EDB, whose authored self\-description graphs ride on gmeow:stage\-source\-load \(read, never re\-loaded\)\. The opaque fanout members \(references, bench, agreement matrix, apache config, matrix, eval/research\-object sidecars, metadata void/dcat\) ride in from their producing export leaves — rendered once, in the leaf, never re\-rendered in the terminal \(the transform\-once razor\)\.

